# Rust build artefacts
/target/

# Local cache: scratch build trees, audit worktrees and other working
# residuals. Unanchored on purpose: a scratch directory created at the
# wrong depth is still a residual, and Cargo.toml's `exclude` already
# drops `.cache/` at any depth. Never contains anything the crate needs;
# safe to delete at any time.
.cache/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.phaios-venv/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# maturin / extension module outputs
*.so
*.pyd

# Generated example outputs (PPM files are regenerated on each run)
examples/output/*.ppm

# Development tooling — not part of the crate
claude-md-templates/
design-briefs/
phaios-core.code-workspace

# Editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store

# Criterion benchmark artefacts
criterion/

# kernel-viewer tool: build artefacts, and everything in testdata/ except
# the files re-included at the end of the image block below. The
# directory's contents are ignored rather than the directory itself,
# because git cannot re-include a file below an ignored directory.
tools/kernel-viewer/target/
/tools/kernel-viewer/testdata/*

# Image assets are never committed (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Examples"): the
# test image is built in code, and a real photograph in the tree could
# ship to both registries. One bracket-class pattern per format, because
# git ignore patterns are case-sensitive and cameras write upper-case
# extensions. Three layers enforce the rule: these lines, the "No image
# assets" step in CI (which sees tracked files, so it catches a
# `git add -f`), and Cargo.toml's `exclude`. The one exception is
# re-included by name pattern at the end of this block.
*.[Dd][Nn][Gg]
*.[Nn][Ee][Ff]
*.[Cc][Rr]2
*.[Cc][Rr]3
*.[Aa][Rr][Ww]
*.[Rr][Aa][Ff]
*.[Oo][Rr][Ff]
*.[Rr][Ww]2
*.[Pp][Ee][Ff]
*.[Ss][Rr][Ww]
*.[Jj][Pp][Gg]
*.[Jj][Pp][Ee][Gg]
*.[Pp][Nn][Gg]
*.[Tt][Ii][Ff]
*.[Tt][Ii][Ff][Ff]
*.[Ww][Ee][Bb][Pp]
*.[Hh][Ee][Ii][Cc]
*.[Hh][Ee][Ii][Ff]
*.[Bb][Mm][Pp]
*.[Gg][Ii][Ff]
*.[Ee][Xx][Rr]
*.[Hh][Dd][Rr]
*.[Pp][Gg][Mm]
*.[Pp][Bb][Mm]
*.[Pp][Pp][Mm]
*.[Pp][Ss][Dd]
# The one exception: the maintainer's test photographs, the camera's own
# JPEG of each where the RAW embeds one, and their README
# (tools/kernel-viewer/testdata/). Only the normalised names are
# re-included, photoNN.<dng|arw|nef> and photoNN.camera.jpg, so stray
# files and sidecars beside them stay ignored. This is convenience, not
# the gate: CI accepts only the files listed, with their checksums, in
# that README, so a correctly named photograph that is not listed still
# fails. Cargo.toml's `exclude` keeps them out of the crate and the
# sdist, and .gitattributes out of source archives.
!/tools/kernel-viewer/testdata/README.md
!/tools/kernel-viewer/testdata/photo[0-9][0-9].dng
!/tools/kernel-viewer/testdata/photo[0-9][0-9].arw
!/tools/kernel-viewer/testdata/photo[0-9][0-9].nef
!/tools/kernel-viewer/testdata/photo[0-9][0-9].camera.jpg

# Claude Code's per-project directory (settings, worktrees, session
# state). It lives in the working tree but is never part of the crate and
# must not be picked up by a `git add -A`; Cargo.toml's `exclude` keeps
# it out of the package as well, in case it is ever tracked deliberately.
.claude/
